From cb5ab8deba8dd2cde3f213625a8a4cc5cb4f67e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: moWerk <mo@mowerk.net>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 19:39:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 51/51] arm64: dts: qcom: sm6115-pro1x: route the SPMI
 interrupt through the MPM
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

In system sleep the GIC is off and only interrupts that reach the MPM
wake the phone. The SPMI arbiter carries the power key, the RTC alarms
and the USB-C attach; without this a plugged-in cable was seen only
868 s later. As on agatti, pin 86.

Disclosure: LLMGD-2 · origin O1 (the model wrote it; built and tested on the device by the model)
LLMGD: v0.3; assurance=A2; flags=T; origin=O1; origin_headline=O1; scope=kernel; graded-by=model; retrieval=none
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115-fxtec-pro1x.dts | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115-fxtec-pro1x.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115-fxtec-pro1x.dts
index 789bc0e4c..66ea921fb 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115-fxtec-pro1x.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115-fxtec-pro1x.dts
@@ -1686,6 +1686,15 @@ system_pd: power-domain-system {
 	};
 };
 
+/*
+ * In system sleep the GIC is off: an interrupt wakes the phone only if it reaches the MPM.
+ * The SPMI arbiter carries the power key, the RTC alarms and the USB-C attach (as on agatti).
+ * TSENS is left on the GIC: the downstream pin 2 maps to GIC 190, sm6115's TSENS is SPI 275.
+ */
+&spmi_bus {
+	interrupts-extended = <&mpm 86 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+};
+
 &cluster_0_pd {
 	power-domains = <&system_pd>;
 };
